# How each creature actually moves, measured one room at a time. Keyed by
# (level, slot in SPIDERS[level - 1]) ->
#   (bob_travel_px, bob_half_period_frames, frames_per_pose)
#
# The travel runs DOWNWARDS from the y in SPIDERS, which is the top row of
# the box the creature was measured in - so a measured creature is drawn
# exactly where the ROM draws it. An unmeasured slot falls back to the
# archetype amplitudes in HeroConstants instead.
#
# Creatures are NOT all animated at one rate. Level 2's two bobbing spiders
# fall 9 px and climb back over exactly 64 frames while alternating two
# bitmaps every 8; a bat patrols about 22 px over ~184 frames and holds each
# wing pose for 4; and most creatures never move at all - level 1's spider
# and level 2's other two hang dead still. Levels 4-16 still run on the
# archetype defaults until each of them is remeasured.
