#
# This is the difference between a creature that is still and one that only
# happens not to travel. CHARACTERS.md: "whether a creature moves is a
# property of the room, not of the creature - 33 of 44 bats and 39 of 50
# spiders are completely stationary", and a stationary one is drawn as ONE
# bitmap, not as a pose cycle someone forgot to stop. Without this the pose
# clock keeps running for a creature the ROM never redraws, so a spider that
# the census saw hold a single shape for the whole scan still swapped its
# legs every eight frames on screen.
#
# The count is the census's `distinct_sprites` (level_images/hero_entities.py)
# capped at the number of poses the kind has art for, so it selects between
