# Magma mouths: a corridor gap between two magma walls that the magma closes
# over and opens again. Measured on level 14 room 5 (2026-09-24): while the
# hero is alive the magma on each side grows one 4-px cell over the gap every
# `step` frames until the gap is shut, then draws back, n = w / 4 steps to the
# cycle, and the cycle starts from the frame the room is ENTERED (four arrival
# times gave the identical sequence). With e frames since entry the magma on
# each side is
#
#     half - |((e + shift) // step) % n - half|        cells, half = n / 2
#
# It burns like any magma. After a death in the room it stays fully OPEN for
# the rest of that visit; the next entry starts the cycle again. Fitted by
# tools/hero_gen/build_level.py (mouths()) to every frame of a 256-frame watch.
# per level: [(room, gap x, gap w, step, shift)]
